<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  The widget extension's entitlements. ONE key, and it exists so the extension can read the
  per-device credential the containing app minted into the Keychain — see
  DeviceSecretReader.swift for the whole mechanism, and the alanwalton-app program's
  entitlements for the app's side of the same group.

  The group is the APP's identifier, not the widget's. That is what sharing means here: the
  item lives in the app's domain and this target is admitted to it. Naming the widget's own
  bundle id would create a second, empty domain and every tile would draw refused.

  The array is empty here because the group is a value the app's page has. The widget-target
  seam fills it in from NATIVE_SHELL_KEYCHAIN_ACCESS_GROUP as it copies this file into the
  generated project and wires it to CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS.

  NOTHING TO PROVISION. There is no keychain capability in the App Store Connect enumeration
  and every profile already grants the team prefix, so this needs no bundleIdCapabilities
  call and no profile regeneration.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>keychain-access-groups</key>
	<array/>
</dict>
</plist>
